{
  "name": "rattlesnake",
  "_about": "SCULPTED (2026-11-21, tools/creaturegen/rework/herps/snakes.py): the WESTERN DIAMONDBACK RATTLESNAKE, Crotalus atrox, 1.4 m and heavy (6 cm thick); the PIT VIPER'S HEAD: broad and triangular at the jowls on a thin neck, the crown in small scales, the brow shields jutting over the eyes (vertical pupils), the canthus edge down to a narrow snout, the HEAT PIT between eye and nostril, two pale lines down the face; dark DIAMONDS with paler centres, edged cream, down the back, dark blotches on the flanks; the tail ringed black and white; THE RATTLE: eight stacked horny segments, each a lobed ring over the next. Coats: western diamondback, red diamond, Mojave.",
